// A change of the window's size wakes `<<|` with `⤢` (D-17, GAP-ZYE-012).
//
// ptydrive.py changes the pty's size with no key sent; the kernel tells the
// program with SIGWINCH. Each line printed is the key `<<|` returned, its
// modifiers, and what `>>?` answers after it: 10530 is `⤢`, and the size must
// be the new one. Before D-17 the program learned nothing until `q`.
>>| {
    @ {
        <<| k, m
        ? k == 'q' { @! }
        (h, w) = >>?
        >> "key " 0d|k| " m " m " size " h "x" w ¶
    }
}
